From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:11:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(allwinner): restart the watchdog count in system reset

sunxi_system_reset() sets the watchdog to reset the system after its
shortest timeout, then waits for it. When the OS left the watchdog
running, as Linux does on a panic or an emergency restart, the counter
has already passed that timeout and the reset never comes: the call
panics with "PSCI: System reset failed" and the board hangs until
power is cut. Restart the count after setting the timeout, as Linux's
own sunxi-wdt restart handler does.

---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 28abd3c..056cd86 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #define SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_REG		(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0010)
 #define SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG		(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0014)
 #define SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG		(SUNXI_R_WDOG_BASE + 0x0018)
+#define SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_RELOAD		((0xa57 << 1) | 1)
 
 static int sunxi_pwr_domain_on(u_register_t mpidr)
 {
@@ -58,6 +59,11 @@ static void __dead2 sunxi_system_reset(void)
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG, 1);
 	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
+	/*
+	 * Restart the count: a watchdog the OS left running has counted past
+	 * the new timeout, and would never fire.
+	 */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_REG, SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_RELOAD);
 	/* Wait for twice the watchdog timeout before panicking */
 	mdelay(1000);
 
-- 
